"relation":"supersedes","target_id":"7b97-0033-3ea5-4aef"},{"link_uuid":"3e743d6c-d11d-4cc0-a0cd-b3ae0dd2b079","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"ffe5-87ef-0351-495b"},{"link_uuid":"b658fc90-b6aa-42cf-bff7-6adddb097f27","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"b2b9-c03f-79d0-473d"},{"link_uuid":"c1ff4f6d-3b9e-41b7-bce4-691d9532c0ca","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"e4e6-8d0a-4c37-4e25"},{"link_uuid":"3582516b-4bfa-40cc-892b-89ee6b7a851e","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"0a2f-a198-877a-432d"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\nThe .github/workflows cohort contains audited comments or docstrings that obscure current behavior with repetition, obvious narration, duplicated explanation, or historical detail. The audit is pinned to `9e65567b79ffe872534c3c656ade7b34340d8192`.\n\n## Approach\nEdit explanatory text only in this directory/subsystem cohort. Condense it to current, non-obvious rationale and constraints; retain every file-specific preserve item and consumer contract below. Grouping adjacent files from one subsystem keeps the change reviewable in one session and permits one coherent verification pass without changing executable behavior.\n\n## Scope\n- `.github/workflows/_artifact-probe.yml:3-18` — Preserve reusable in mirror and Gerrit lanes; builds sdist then wheel; verifies package probes and embedded commit; no secrets. Consumer: GitHub Actions.\n- `.github/workflows/_build-and-test.yml:3-20,104-119,125-129,139-158,168-180,189-208,221-245,301-314,427-459,483-531,769-835,843-853,868-929` — Preserve lane/ref behavior, security boundaries, skew guards, sandbox posture, dependency ownership policy, timeout semantics, exact matrix selection, shallow-checkout caveats, and blocking/advisory status. Consumer: GitHub Actions and repository-policy tests.\n- `.github/workflows/_eval-discipline.yml:3-16,67-74` — Preserve reusable offline gate, two callers, no secrets/model calls, 300-second per-test guard. Consumer: GitHub Actions.\n- `.github/workflows/_mutation.yml:59-64,124-129,137-147` — Preserve bubblewrap is unavailable on hosted Ubuntu due to namespace policy; this explicitly approved lane is unsandboxed only because the runner is ephemeral. Consumer: GitHub Actions/mutation gate.\n- `.github/workflows/_optionality.yml:3-22,87-90,98-107,122-132,144-158,177-203,244-249,267-281` — Preserve two callers, patchset checkout behavior, per-file presence guards, no-extra degradation checks, isolated per-extra environments, union resolution, absolute interpreter paths, and aggregated failures. Consumer: GitHub Actions/optionality tests.\n- `.github/workflows/codeql.yml:3-19` — Preserve public-mirror SAST, scheduled six-hour scan, manual dispatch, no push trigger. Consumer: GitHub Actions.\n- `.github/workflows/compact-sweep.yml:1-25,55-59,147-152,162-165` — Preserve out-of-band full-history compaction, union-safe merge, single flight, bounded job, exit-2 policy, metrics. Consumer: GitHub Actions/operators.\n- `.github/workflows/dependency-advisory-canary.yml:1-26` — Preserve daily high/critical audit, one deduplicated ticket, daily comment cap, release-only blocking. Consumer: GitHub Actions.\n- `.github/workflows/external-integration.yml:3-35,49-80,161-168,199-241,369-401,478-552,588-622,636-657,757-805,891-904` — Preserve manual/billable boundaries, provider isolation, credential and OIDC mapping, timeout calibration, test partitioning/canaries, cleanup guarantees, artifact output. Consumer: GitHub Actions/live integration operators.\n- `.github/workflows/gerrit-verify.yaml:3-22,211-219,242-291,340-347,397-407,428-459,519-557` — Preserve exact patchset checkout, required jobs/vote dependencies, authenticated authorship, normalization source, conclusion mapping, observability-only behavior. Consumer: GitHub Actions/Gerrit vote bot.\n- `.github/workflows/jira-dc-capability-map.yml:3-20,52-59,71-74,94-97` — Preserve manual diagnostic, pinned shared Jira image, one batched agent run, evidence artifact, no mutation, required LLM extra. Consumer: GitHub Actions/operators.\n- `.github/workflows/jira-dc-epic-link-probe.yml:3-24` — Preserve manual deterministic Jira DC probe, scope, output/evidence, non-mutation. Consumer: GitHub Actions/operators.\n- `.github/workflows/jira-dc-exact-patchset.yml:3-29,56-67,130-133,158-170` — Preserve exact Gerrit patchset, recorded SHA/ref, isolated before/after DC runs, required extra, artifact evidence. Consumer: GitHub Actions/operators.\n- `.github/workflows/jira-dc-richtext-probe.yml:3-21,53-56,93-99` — Preserve manual read-only diagnostic, shared pinned harness, required extras, direct-Anthropic overlay, evidence artifact. Consumer: GitHub Actions/operators.\n- `.github/workflows/mirror-guard.yml:3-20` — Preserve scheduled persistent-divergence check, sample window, public reads/default token, ruleset drift excluded. Consumer: GitHub Actions/operators.\n- `.github/workflows/optionality.yml:3-19` — Preserve caller purpose and why `main` is schedule-only. Consumer: GitHub Actions.\n- `.github/workflows/prompt-eval.yml:3-27,44-50,132-136` — Preserve offline reusable gate versus billable eval job, schedule/dispatch behavior, token record. Consumer: GitHub Actions.\n- `.github/workflows/reconcile-bridge-canary.yml:1-31,80-86,133-160,194-198` — Preserve heartbeat threshold, dedup ticket lifecycle, signing key route, non-exempt authoring, full-history tickets worktree, binding parity. Consumer: GitHub Actions/rebar canary.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Every listed location contains only current, non-obvious rationale or constraints after remediation; verified by reviewing the final diff against every Scope row.\n- [ ] Every preserve item in Scope remains explicit and accurate; verified by the row-by-row completion comment.\n- [ ] Every consumer contract in Scope remains explicit and accurate; verified by the row-by-row completion comment.\n- [ ] No executable behavior changes; verified by inspecting the final diff and running the command under Verification.\n- [ ] No test assertion changes; verified by inspecting the final diff.\n\n## Verification\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make lint`\n\nThe row-by-row diff review is authoritative for prose quality; the hygiene guard detects only its narrow deterministic history-token rule.","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[{"path":".github/workflows/_artifact-probe.yml","reason":"Condense comments/docstrings while preserving the scoped contract."},{"path":".github/workflows/_build-and-test.yml","reason":"Condense comments/docstrings while preserving the scoped contract."},{"path":".github/workflows/_eval-discipline.yml","reason":"Condense comments/docstrings while preserving the scoped contract."},{"path":".github/workflows/_mutation.yml","reason":"Condense comments/docstrings while preserving the scoped contract."},{"path":".github/workflows/_optionality.yml","reason":"Condense comments/docstrings while preserving the scoped contract."},{"path":".github/workflows/codeql.yml","reason":"Condense comments/docstrings while preserving the scoped contract."},{"path":".github/workflows/compact-sweep.yml","reason":"Condense comments/docstrings while preserving the scoped contract."},{"path":".github/workflows/dependency-advisory-canary.yml","reason":"Condense comments/docstrings while preserving the scoped contract."},{"path":".github/workflows/external-integration.yml","reason":"Condense comments/docstrings while preserving the scoped contract."},{"path":".github/workflows/gerrit-verify.yaml","reason":"Condense comments/docstrings while preserving the scoped contract."},{"path":".github/workflows/jira-dc-capability-map.yml","reason":"Condense comments/docstrings while preserving the scoped contract."},{"path":".github/workflows/jira-dc-epic-link-probe.yml","reason":"Condense comments/docstrings while preserving the scoped contract."},{"path":".github/workflows/jira-dc-exact-patchset.yml","reason":"Condense comments/docstrings while preserving the s